WEBVTT

00:02.100 --> 00:02.480
2

00:02.100 --> 00:02.480
3

00:02.980 --> 00:03.100
2

00:07.000 --> 00:09.610
The story so far.

00:09.610 --> 00:13.480
Mammonism envelops the world.
A money game where money makes money.

00:13.480 --> 00:18.780
Having lost $10,000,000 with one click,
I was driven from my position as a money changer.

00:18.780 --> 00:22.610
Wandering the city in the depths of failure,
a lone girl struck up a conversation with me.

00:23.030 --> 00:26.150
Asking to be “bought for 30 Zimbabwe dollars!”

00:26.150 --> 00:29.160
I replied that I lacked such a currency.

00:29.160 --> 00:33.420
She then asked for “20,000,000 yen”.

00:33.420 --> 00:36.200
Isn't that rate a bit off? It's a sudden price hike.

00:36.200 --> 00:42.000
As I corrected her, a man from behind me said “no, the girl's right.”

00:42.000 --> 00:48.810
A gentleman who described himself as looking like
Hamasho appeared. “I'll show you the real money game”,
he said, and led me to where people are traded.

00:48.810 --> 00:50.680
The Human Trade Center.

00:50.680 --> 00:56.570
“At the current rate, one Anglo-Saxon trades for
107 of the Yamato race”, said a fund manager.

00:56.570 --> 01:02.050
“Absurd! Are not all men equal!?” Nozomu remarked indignantly.

01:02.050 --> 01:06.740
“Japanese are relatively expensive. There are far cheaper races.”

01:06.740 --> 01:12.450
Told “Equality is nothing but a fantasy. Get
to work”, he was forced into a seat.

01:12.450 --> 01:15.620
One click sold a million men. He couldn't!

01:15.620 --> 01:19.740
But shown the rate curve, he soon reflexively clicked.

01:19.740 --> 01:25.190
With the click of the mouse came a roaring jet sound.

01:25.190 --> 01:27.550
I've lost again.

01:27.550 --> 01:31.100
With one click, I've lost ten million men.

01:31.100 --> 01:35.800
That mouse was the red button of destruction.

01:35.800 --> 01:42.070
“It's the kind of story summary a middle schooler would write!”

01:43.850 --> 01:45.650
Released by Sandwich-anime

03:17.480 --> 03:21.610
Golden Week this year has a midweek holiday.

03:21.850 --> 03:22.030
I've had enough

03:22.030 --> 03:22.200
But letting the quality down
isn't very nice to the viewers

03:22.200 --> 03:22.350
I want the rest of my work off my schedule

03:22.350 --> 03:22.530
But once I've cut it off
they won't take me back

03:22.530 --> 03:22.700
I want a higher budget

03:22.700 --> 03:22.950
But Ghostory is what sells

03:23.200 --> 03:26.850
Network of the Proletariat

03:23.200 --> 03:26.850
From Chapter 136

03:23.200 --> 03:26.850
Originally published April 23, Showa 83.

03:27.980 --> 03:29.990
There is a midweek holiday.

03:29.990 --> 03:31.190
Holiday?

03:31.720 --> 03:36.620
No, if you ask the workers, it is a midholiday workweek!

03:36.620 --> 03:40.320
And there's the worker's holiday, May Day!

03:40.320 --> 03:43.530
I can almost hear Bloodshed at the Amur River!

03:44.770 --> 03:47.640
You see! You can really hear them.

03:47.800 --> 03:51.140
We demand a salary increase!

03:52.840 --> 03:55.180
Ooh, it's a demonstration!

03:56.610 --> 03:59.430
Aren't you all excited?

03:59.430 --> 04:00.900
You're a leftist, right?

04:00.900 --> 04:03.360
I'm not a leftist, I'm a teacher.

04:05.320 --> 04:07.770
Anyway, what's this demonstration about?

04:09.320 --> 04:12.500
Unfortunately, this isn't a demonstration.

04:12.500 --> 04:14.300
It's a vacillation.

04:15.860 --> 04:18.270
It looks like a demonstration.

04:18.270 --> 04:19.890
It's a vacillation.

04:19.890 --> 04:22.340
Raise our salaries!

04:22.340 --> 04:24.340
Raise our salaries!

04:24.570 --> 04:30.340
But... if the company spends too much on personnel,
there will be another round of restructuring.

04:31.490 --> 04:32.910
Oh, so that's what you mean!

04:32.910 --> 04:35.000
Strike!

04:35.000 --> 04:38.220
But taking time off would hurt our customers!

04:40.860 --> 04:44.740
Even if Japanese, with no decisiveness or
solidarity, want to hold a demonstration,

04:44.740 --> 04:49.030
somehow it always becomes vacillation!

04:49.030 --> 04:56.540
That's right. On May 1st, along with
demonstrating, the entire country vacillates!

04:58.650 --> 05:02.680
It's happening over there too. They're vacillating.

05:02.680 --> 05:04.680
About what?

05:06.960 --> 05:09.050
It seems like anti-Japanese Vacillation.

05:09.330 --> 05:12.430
Even about that!? ... And they're doing it on Japanese soil!?

05:12.430 --> 05:14.220
Down with Japan!

05:14.660 --> 05:18.360
But I like some of their anime and manga.

05:18.730 --> 05:20.340
I see...

05:20.600 --> 05:23.580
What are they vacillating about?

05:23.580 --> 05:26.620
They want the liberation of Akihabara.

05:26.620 --> 05:29.440
Freedom for Akihabara!

05:30.460 --> 05:33.650
But... we're already free enough.

05:34.630 --> 05:38.880
They're vacillating to protect the town's scenic nature.

05:38.880 --> 05:41.580
New houses will ruin the beautiful views!

05:41.580 --> 05:43.390
Don't build them!

05:44.380 --> 05:48.330
But only the last two, the rest are fine.

05:48.330 --> 05:52.070
They're vacillating about so many things.

05:52.070 --> 05:53.970
But!

05:53.970 --> 05:57.070
Yes... demonstrations lead to vacillation.

05:59.840 --> 06:03.840
Vacillation leading to collapses in support have left me in despair!

06:01.650 --> 06:03.840
• Against demolishing old apartments, but they're dangerous in earthquakes
• Against dipping into social security but has a pension
• Against the digital TV changeover, but doesn't watch much TV
• Wants a higher allowance but already in their 20s
• Against building new highways but wants one to Miyazaki
• Against internet censorship but doesn't want their info online
• Against the Giants headhunting players from other teams but they're not actually that great
• Against fur, but likes Meatel's outfit

06:06.340 --> 06:09.880
These vacillations are scary.

06:09.880 --> 06:11.100
You were there?

06:11.100 --> 06:12.650
Yes, always.

06:12.650 --> 06:15.740
No to the new power plant!

06:15.740 --> 06:18.550
Think of the people's safety!

06:19.220 --> 06:24.590
But what if there's a brownout late
at night while I'm watching anime?

06:24.590 --> 06:30.400
Just one vacillation can spread to everyone on the route!

06:30.640 --> 06:33.210
But late-night anime is shitty.

06:33.210 --> 06:35.640
But To Love-Ru is good.

06:35.640 --> 06:38.850
But Minami-ke Okawari is better.

06:38.850 --> 06:41.090
But not as good as Clannad.

06:42.640 --> 06:45.380
It's turned into nothing but vacillation!

06:46.630 --> 06:48.780
It really is fearsome,

06:48.780 --> 06:51.120
but nothing will come of it.

06:51.120 --> 06:57.690
Now that I think of it, we go on sale April 23rd.
Isn't that a bit early for a May Day gag?

06:59.080 --> 07:02.740
It's a double issue, so if we don't do it this week...

07:02.740 --> 07:05.570
the next issue isn't until May 7th.

07:06.510 --> 07:10.310
But it's still pushing it.

07:12.050 --> 07:15.550
But you don't need to go that far to match the season.

07:15.550 --> 07:17.420
But!

07:18.490 --> 07:20.050
What is this!?

07:20.050 --> 07:21.150
Oh no!

07:21.350 --> 07:24.020
Teacher, you're leading the demonstration!

07:27.020 --> 07:30.160
You vacillated!

07:30.160 --> 07:37.150
But don't worry! Freedom of assembly is guaranteed
under the Japanese constitution!

07:37.560 --> 07:40.060
Don't say I'm leading the demonstration!

07:40.060 --> 07:42.830
You'll ruin my reputation!

07:43.780 --> 07:46.510
What if undercover agents come after me again?

07:47.020 --> 07:53.020
It's really scary. I didn't even realize
that I was starting a vacillation!

07:53.870 --> 07:58.410
It must be nice to have such leadership skills.

07:58.890 --> 08:03.590
That's right. Teacher always says “but” and “however”.

08:03.590 --> 08:06.600
Don't talk about me like I'm a little kid!

08:06.600 --> 08:11.640
I'd like to use your skills to break up the demonstration.

08:11.830 --> 08:14.710
You say that, but how?

08:15.030 --> 08:17.380
Who are you, anyway?

08:18.490 --> 08:21.810
Here comes another demonstration!

08:23.480 --> 08:28.620
Don't give the Olympics to oppressive countries! Boycott them!

08:31.320 --> 08:35.220
Oh, this is a nice demonstration. I completely agree.

08:35.530 --> 08:36.960
We must boycott them!

08:38.750 --> 08:41.330
But what about the poor athletes?

08:42.710 --> 08:48.650
True, it's not their fault.

08:48.650 --> 08:50.740
Politics and sport are different matters.

08:51.140 --> 08:53.980
But still, we must boycott them!

08:53.980 --> 08:57.090
But we've already bought the broadcast rights.

08:57.090 --> 09:00.180
But we've already paid sponsorship money.

09:00.370 --> 09:03.420
But someone's finally interested in me.

09:03.420 --> 09:06.270
But I've invested in Chinese stocks.

09:06.620 --> 09:08.860
I want to watch the Olympics!

09:08.860 --> 09:11.350
I want to support the Japanese competitors!

09:11.350 --> 09:15.270
It's completely changed from demonstration to vacillation!

09:15.490 --> 09:18.190
What a cowardly way to manipulate public opinion!

09:18.190 --> 09:22.510
It's nothing more than propaganda for
special-interest groups and traitorous politicians!

09:24.220 --> 09:25.110
What?

09:25.510 --> 09:29.850
Teacher, you're a socialist!

09:32.310 --> 09:35.060
Stop it! Don't call me a socialist!

09:35.060 --> 09:37.390
That's always an insult when you say it in gag comedies!

09:37.760 --> 09:41.600
This kind of serious demonstration is good if you do it assertively,

09:41.600 --> 09:44.430
but isn't there a more tepid demonstration somewhere?

09:45.220 --> 09:48.170
Maria participated in a lot of demonstrations.

09:49.170 --> 09:52.900
Demonstrations in your country are too serious!

09:52.900 --> 09:55.910
In Japan. I'm Japanese, after all.

10:01.980 --> 10:05.260
Maria has bad balance when she wears shoes.

10:05.690 --> 10:07.290
You're terrible.

10:07.290 --> 10:10.190
But you're cute, so I'll forgive you.

10:10.190 --> 10:12.190
Oh no! My suit!

10:12.190 --> 10:15.030
But you're cute, so I'll forgive you.

10:15.030 --> 10:18.050
But you're cute, so I'll forgive you.

10:18.050 --> 10:20.220
What's with this vacillation!?

10:20.220 --> 10:22.030
Well, I guess it is tepid.

10:22.230 --> 10:26.410
Don't think you'll be forgiven
for anything just because you're cute.

10:30.560 --> 10:32.740
This is an international incident!

10:40.910 --> 10:43.970
But you're cute, so I'll forgive you.

10:47.150 --> 10:49.480
Good job, Maria-chan.

10:51.160 --> 10:52.670
What publishers have to say

10:52.670 --> 10:56.130
What publishers have to say

10:53.420 --> 10:56.130
So can you tell us anything?

10:56.130 --> 10:59.400
One of the editors helped me out a lot.

10:59.400 --> 11:03.060
But didn't they treat you horribly?

11:03.060 --> 11:06.710
They're treating my former staff great.

11:08.450 --> 11:11.820
... But they didn't make an anime for me.

11:11.820 --> 11:15.550
But they didn't print my first serialization in colour.

11:15.550 --> 11:18.290
But they're not reprinting anything.

11:15.550 --> 11:18.290
What publishers have to say

11:18.890 --> 11:20.680
That's all.

11:18.990 --> 11:19.110
What publishers have to say

11:20.680 --> 11:24.270
But my rate went up 5000 yen a page when I came here.

11:24.270 --> 11:25.170
But!

11:39.110 --> 11:41.090
This book is very popular, isn't it.

11:41.090 --> 11:45.120
Yeah. Lately, novels by Kyoto Uni grads have been pretty popular.

11:50.920 --> 11:53.150
Is that an interesting one, Nami-chan?

11:55.580 --> 11:57.230
It's amazing.

11:57.230 --> 11:59.930
The text, overflowing with wisdom, flows like music.

11:59.930 --> 12:02.320
It's as if the letters are dancing in a musical.

12:02.320 --> 12:03.840
It's the best!

12:04.280 --> 12:05.250
... I see.

12:05.250 --> 12:06.740
May I interject?

12:06.740 --> 12:08.740
The story may be interesting,

12:08.740 --> 12:12.640
but the writing is very pretentious.

12:13.090 --> 12:15.940
It intentionally uses difficult phrases and expressions.

12:15.940 --> 12:20.950
If you say it's hard to read or dull,
doesn't that make you look stupid?

12:23.050 --> 12:26.720
Somehow, it feels like you <i>have</i> to say it's interesting.

12:26.730 --> 12:26.900
Moon Phase

12:26.900 --> 12:27.070
Paniponi

12:27.070 --> 12:27.240
Negima!?

12:27.240 --> 12:27.410
Hidamari

12:27.410 --> 12:27.580
Zetsubou-sensei

12:27.580 --> 12:27.830
Shinbo Akiyuki x SHAFT

12:28.000 --> 12:31.750
Time for oddities, girls

12:28.000 --> 12:31.750
From Chapter 185

12:28.000 --> 12:31.750
Originally published June 10, Showa 84.

12:32.420 --> 12:38.470
It's not just books. In this world, there are many
things where it seems one must feign interest.

12:45.520 --> 12:48.550
Wow! This is great!

12:48.550 --> 12:51.300
Like comedies where you feel like you have to laugh...

12:51.300 --> 12:55.150
and the joke is on the people that aren't refined enough to!

12:55.150 --> 12:57.650
Why are you using me as the example!?

12:57.650 --> 13:01.050
Fools simply accept the judgment of their betters,

13:01.050 --> 13:04.660
and act as if they're the best!

13:09.160 --> 13:10.900
Yes... thus...

13:13.830 --> 13:17.810
This is nothing but unconditional
gratitude for the gifts of heaven!

13:17.810 --> 13:19.670
It's unconditional happiness!

13:20.030 --> 13:22.180
Oh, I know a great example.

13:24.430 --> 13:27.750
Didn't we go to a museum the other day?

13:29.650 --> 13:31.750
This piece is interesting.

13:31.750 --> 13:33.760
I like this one.

13:33.760 --> 13:35.980
It's very modern.

13:35.980 --> 13:36.760
This one's good.

13:36.760 --> 13:38.500
Nami-chan, that's a humidifier.

13:40.370 --> 13:42.430
Yeah, that makes it clear.

13:42.430 --> 13:45.370
I said, why do you always have to use me as the example!?

13:45.370 --> 13:47.370
Wrong. This is...

13:49.590 --> 13:51.710
the legendary Oh ball!

13:52.470 --> 13:53.970
Oh ball?

13:53.970 --> 13:57.450
When Oh played, since he was
one of the great batters of the era,

13:57.450 --> 14:03.690
umpires assumed that if he let
a pitch go by, it had to be a ball.

14:03.880 --> 14:05.000
Ball!

14:05.000 --> 14:06.760
And called it.

14:06.760 --> 14:10.900
Is having one's reputation held so highly a success?

14:10.900 --> 14:11.990
Correct!

14:12.210 --> 14:14.410
With enough brand power,

14:14.410 --> 14:19.000
even just an emperor penguin
knit can be called fashionable!

14:21.770 --> 14:25.600
Oh, what wonderful, legendary Oh balls!

14:25.350 --> 14:26.650
• That former Blue Samurai's killer pass where the receiver who misses it is wrong
• That best-selling comic with the fatal misprint
• That 16-Mon kick you have to pretend is damaging
• German luxury cars where the more expensive ones sell better
• The Booksellers Prize winner that you have to call interesting
• 50,000 Yen opera tickets that you have to call worth 50,000 Yen
• Actresses who make a role like Bon actually look pretty cool

14:26.650 --> 14:29.040
Wow, no one else has done that in a while.

14:29.040 --> 14:33.410
It's certainly useful to be assumed right.

14:33.410 --> 14:34.550
You were there?

14:34.550 --> 14:35.880
Yes, always.

14:36.270 --> 14:38.890
We should consider developing unclear arms.

14:38.890 --> 14:41.130
That's crazy talk!

14:41.130 --> 14:42.860
Unclear. I said unclear.

14:42.860 --> 14:44.960
That's impossible.

14:44.960 --> 14:46.360
We don't have anything to be pretentious about.

14:46.360 --> 14:50.670
The point is, we need to create an atmosphere
where one feels one must laugh.

14:52.100 --> 14:57.340
Hey, what's your opinion on the Eretrian
school's thesis of affirmation!?

15:02.750 --> 15:05.270
What's that supposed to mean?

15:07.420 --> 15:10.230
Eretrian is a funny word.

15:11.450 --> 15:13.220
My tummy hurts now!

15:16.760 --> 15:18.200
I don't understand the meaning,

15:18.200 --> 15:20.500
but it's definitely funny!

15:20.500 --> 15:23.500
If I don't laugh, I'll look dumb.

15:24.090 --> 15:25.780
The E... Erelarela school...

15:28.440 --> 15:29.300
That's it.

15:29.300 --> 15:33.780
We must make learned-seeming gags that
the viewer will feel the need to laugh at!

15:33.780 --> 15:37.780
Really, I think they're more low-minded.

15:38.150 --> 15:39.510
Even if we can't have unclear weapons,

15:39.510 --> 15:41.290
we can have incomprehensible ones.

15:41.520 --> 15:46.290
If we look in the dictionary or technical books,
we can find unusual, difficult words.

15:46.290 --> 15:48.430
Let's give it a try.

15:49.240 --> 15:52.770
Last night I went to Joji's shop and got a chocolate drink.

15:53.080 --> 15:54.400
That's unusual.

15:54.590 --> 15:57.130
It's like Sartre carrying a portable shrine!

16:02.470 --> 16:06.480
You said it because of how annoying the Frankfurt school is.

16:06.650 --> 16:11.220
Your mother is Maria Theresa! Maria Theresa! Maria Theresa!

16:12.120 --> 16:14.930
Oh yeah! Your mother is Maria Sergio!

16:17.360 --> 16:19.590
C'mon, what are you trying to do,
make Celibidache direct traffic!?

16:21.530 --> 16:24.160
You're all such erudites.

16:28.730 --> 16:31.740
It's like the Pythagorean educational philosophy.

16:31.740 --> 16:34.630
Perhaps I should drop out and take
night classes from a 17 year cicada.

16:34.630 --> 16:37.370
Hop-Step-Amonhotep III!

16:37.370 --> 16:39.430
He's like a young Einstein.

16:40.340 --> 16:42.230
Relatively reborn.

16:42.230 --> 16:44.680
That's just a pun..

16:44.680 --> 16:46.310
A raccoon Pascal!

16:47.480 --> 16:50.080
What are these people doing?

16:50.080 --> 16:52.060
Acting educated.

16:52.060 --> 16:54.490
Do you have anything to add, Chiri-chan?

16:54.490 --> 16:55.660
Yes.

16:55.660 --> 17:02.800
I'm the very picture of a modern
Pasileio's imprisonment.

17:06.420 --> 17:08.110
Pa... Pasileio's imprisonment...

17:09.070 --> 17:10.310
That's just too funny!

17:17.100 --> 17:18.440
You were supposed to cry!

17:18.720 --> 17:22.330
Can't you tell the difference
between a comedy and a drama!?

17:22.330 --> 17:24.550
There's no way I could!

17:25.410 --> 17:30.130
Everyone, hold on. You're about to be pulled
by a cosmic string attached to a DeLorean.

17:32.960 --> 17:35.340
That was supposed to be funny.

17:47.300 --> 17:49.480
Want to go to the pool, Chiri?

17:50.090 --> 17:52.000
Sorry, I'm busy.

17:55.270 --> 17:58.920
I'm busier during summer vacation
than when I'm at school.

18:15.050 --> 18:17.010
It's such a mess in here!

18:17.010 --> 18:17.180
Looking forward

18:17.180 --> 18:17.350
to steamed

18:17.350 --> 18:17.520
sweet

18:17.520 --> 18:17.690
potato

18:17.690 --> 18:17.860
along with

18:17.860 --> 18:18.110
the children...

18:18.300 --> 18:22.030
Chyichyl and Mytyl

18:18.300 --> 18:22.030
From Chapter 190

18:18.300 --> 18:22.030
Originally published July 29, Showa 84.

18:22.760 --> 18:25.120
It's such a mess in here!

18:25.120 --> 18:26.910
Why are you so untidy, onee-chan!?

18:27.160 --> 18:29.320
I just cleaned in here this morning!

18:34.390 --> 18:37.380
You messed it up while I was still cleaning!

18:37.380 --> 18:39.330
Wasn't on purpose.

18:45.210 --> 18:46.940
The big sister makes a mess,

18:46.940 --> 18:48.820
the little sister cleans it up.

18:48.820 --> 18:50.440
The big sister makes a mess,

18:50.440 --> 18:52.180
the little sister cleans it up.

18:52.180 --> 18:53.820
The big sister makes a mess,

18:53.820 --> 18:55.510
the little sister cleans it up.

18:55.510 --> 18:58.380
Wait, what are you doing!? Why are you even here!?

18:58.380 --> 19:00.780
Well, if you're just throwing it out...

19:00.780 --> 19:04.920
Ever since you came home, I can't even go out with my friends!

19:06.560 --> 19:12.630
I did just fine when I lived alone, but
here I just rely too much on you.

19:12.630 --> 19:15.270
Liar! I saw you!

19:21.210 --> 19:24.080
Wow, the beams are bending.

19:24.080 --> 19:27.380
What? I tidied up before you came.

19:29.230 --> 19:30.880
This is nothing to laugh about!

19:30.880 --> 19:34.150
If you don't clean up after yourself, you can't live here!

19:38.580 --> 19:42.460
My older sister came home for summer vacation.

19:42.460 --> 19:45.090
She's always been good at making a mess.

19:45.760 --> 19:47.160
Thus, her nickname...

19:47.990 --> 19:50.670
Maybe Kita-nee's back?

19:52.060 --> 19:53.840
You shouldn't call people that to their face.

19:54.890 --> 19:59.860
When you said you were too busy to go
to the pool, I figured she might be here.

19:59.860 --> 20:00.910
The pool?

20:02.050 --> 20:02.930
All right.

20:02.930 --> 20:04.150
Let's go to the pool.

20:05.950 --> 20:07.920
No way!

20:08.100 --> 20:10.070
We can't!

20:10.070 --> 20:11.620
C'mon, let's go!

20:16.630 --> 20:18.080
I knew it!

20:18.080 --> 20:20.600
Come on, don't lose your head.

20:20.600 --> 20:24.240
Why are there things floating in here
that shouldn't even be near a pool!?

20:24.240 --> 20:26.440
Some of this stuff doesn't even have a name in Japanese!

20:26.440 --> 20:29.320
I thought I had enough of an eye
on you that you wouldn't litter!

20:29.320 --> 20:32.610
I told you, I'm not the one doing it.

20:32.610 --> 20:35.060
But it follows you!

20:35.060 --> 20:36.430
Really?

20:37.510 --> 20:40.290
C'mon, see? There's no trash over here.

20:40.830 --> 20:41.820
Wrong.

20:41.820 --> 20:43.850
There's the dregs of society.

20:46.910 --> 20:49.860
Yeah, it's me. That accident sure paid off.

20:49.860 --> 20:50.720
Chiri.

20:54.040 --> 20:56.170
The big sister gives a peek!

20:56.170 --> 20:58.070
The little sister dodges!

20:58.070 --> 20:59.830
The big sister gives a peek!

20:59.830 --> 21:01.690
The little sister dodges!

21:01.690 --> 21:03.460
The big sister gives a peek!

21:03.460 --> 21:05.490
The little sister dodges!

21:05.930 --> 21:07.820
You make a good team.

21:07.820 --> 21:08.710
Really?

21:12.450 --> 21:13.210
Oh,

21:14.550 --> 21:15.650
it's Miss Kitsu.

21:20.310 --> 21:22.360
You're littering again, onee-chan!

21:22.980 --> 21:23.810
Who's that?

21:23.810 --> 21:25.300
It's Chiri's onee-san.

21:27.300 --> 21:29.000
A woman who litters...

21:29.000 --> 21:30.040
Kitsu Tane?

21:30.040 --> 21:32.060
The big sister makes a mess,

21:32.060 --> 21:33.740
the little sister cleans it up.

21:35.300 --> 21:39.640
It must be her fault that her onee-san turned out how she did.

21:39.940 --> 21:42.180
No, it's the other way around.

21:45.920 --> 21:48.820
Your scales are getting dirty, Mr. Goldfish.

21:48.820 --> 21:49.720
Yeah.

21:49.720 --> 21:52.220
Let's clean you off with some shampoo!

21:52.220 --> 21:54.220
Don't wash the goldfish!

21:54.220 --> 21:56.530
What's wrong with washing him?

21:56.530 --> 21:57.000
No!

21:57.000 --> 21:58.330
You can't wash him!

22:04.020 --> 22:06.340
Kita-nee jumped into the mud.

22:06.340 --> 22:09.380
If you're going to wash something, wash me!

22:10.470 --> 22:12.220
I see.

22:12.480 --> 22:15.650
She did it to control Kitsu's excesses.

22:19.130 --> 22:24.560
Even I want to dress up all girly and go on a date.

22:32.100 --> 22:35.430
Then why not tonight, my lady?

22:36.110 --> 22:38.870
With a more daring lipstick than normal,

22:38.870 --> 22:41.300
and in high heels.

22:43.100 --> 22:44.410
You're beautiful.

22:46.040 --> 22:48.290
But if I clean up,

22:48.290 --> 22:50.670
my sister will wash her goldfish.

22:51.260 --> 22:54.320
Then why don't you make me dirty?

22:55.320 --> 22:56.990
Oh no!

22:57.160 --> 23:00.390
Chiri-chan is risking her life to remove graffiti!

23:00.390 --> 23:01.150
Huh?

23:07.000 --> 23:09.170
Noooo!

23:16.280 --> 23:17.720
If you're going to wash something,

23:17.720 --> 23:20.440
wash me!

23:21.650 --> 23:23.650
Is this avant-garde art?

23:25.060 --> 23:26.700
Itoshiki Tane.

23:26.700 --> 23:28.550
Itoshi Kitane.

23:30.500 --> 23:32.570
Either way, Kita-nee.

23:32.570 --> 23:34.110
I just can't win.

23:37.680 --> 23:41.350
Let us make you happy

23:41.520 --> 23:44.520
Find the gate

23:44.520 --> 23:49.440
We renovated the shop, Welcome

23:51.070 --> 23:57.290
Your clothing slips off your shoulder

23:57.450 --> 24:03.710
Forget about your daily life for now

24:03.830 --> 24:06.960
Evening dew settles on you

24:10.300 --> 24:16.560
You can have your heart of flesh and blood blue or rare

24:16.560 --> 24:20.350
We got our stories straight,

24:20.350 --> 24:26.150
a habit to spice with poison and lies

24:27.730 --> 24:34.320
Spear dried sadness on your fork

24:34.490 --> 24:39.950
You can leave what you don't like behind, like a kid

24:40.710 --> 24:43.750
Aren't you happy here?

24:43.920 --> 24:47.000
Mouthful by mouthful it heals you

24:47.170 --> 24:53.380
Until next week, I laugh, and wave my hand

24:53.380 --> 24:57.850
One night is all you can afford

25:04.900 --> 25:07.870
This is a work of fiction
Any speculation that the low DVD sales of Zan Sayonara Zetsubou Sensei
negates the chances of a fourth season, and thus more Kitsu Tane,
have not been in any way officially confirmed.

25:08.450 --> 25:11.190
What did you do last week?

25:11.190 --> 25:13.340
I don't remember that far back.

25:13.340 --> 25:14.940
What are you doing this week?

25:14.940 --> 25:16.570
I don't know yet.

25:16.910 --> 25:19.460
Where were you, say, ten years ago?

25:19.460 --> 25:22.530
I was having a brace put on my teeth. And you?

25:22.530 --> 25:24.840
I was naked. Not even wearing briefs.

25:25.290 --> 25:27.250
Three cheers for my weakness.

25:28.040 --> 25:30.040
Let's despair over the next volume too!
